# What COPY . leaves out of the image. It copies every file in the build context, gitignored or not,
# and this repository is public: an image pushed from a working copy would publish whatever
# machine-local state sits in it. So everything .gitignore names is listed here too, and
# scripts/container.test.mjs fails when .gitignore names something this file does not.
.git
**/node_modules
docs/code-plan
**/graphify-out
diagrams

# Machine-local private state and live coordination state (named in .gitignore)
**/vault-index
**/spike-out
**/plans.publish.json
**/plan.issues.json
**/local.config.json
**/pr.registry.json
**/plan.issues.local.json

# Backups, temp files and editor debris (named in .gitignore)
**/.mermaid-tmp
**/*.json.bak
**/*.md.bak
**/.*.tmp-*
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*~
**/*.swp
**/*.swo

# Secrets that .gitignore does not name
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.claude/settings.local.json
**/*.pem
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
